    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="1129" n="1089" xml:id="pg1089"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">783.02/12–851: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Syria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State </hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d625-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Damascus</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-08T13:00:00+02:00">December 8, 1951—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>344. We appreciate Dept’s instructions re recognition new Syrian regime (Deptel
                    312 [<hi rendition="#italic">212</hi>], December 6)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d625-f2"/> and fully endorse line of action set forth. We believe
                    acknowledgement of circular not best means effecting recognition, particularly
                    because it can be easily concerted with other western powers and wld avoid
                    previous situations when French tried steal show.</p>
                <p>Today Asst Army Attaché talked briefly to Shishikli who after brief résumé recent
                    events said “next move is up to you”. With indications that Arab states may
                    shortly act to recognize regime we think immed agreement with British, French
                    and Turks on Dept’s line of action including draft reply to FonOff note highly
                        desirable.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d625-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d625-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d625-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Paris, London, Ankara, Arab capitals, Tel Aviv, Jerusalem, and
                    Tripoli.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d625-f2" n="2" xml:id="d625-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1086">p. 1086</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d625-f3" n="3" xml:id="d625-f3-content">
                <p>In response, the Department of State in telegram 228 to Damascus, December 11,
                    instructed the Legation, subject to agreement by the French, British, and
                    Turkish Ministers in Damascus, to join with them in drafting a simple note
                    acknowledging the Syrian note of December 3, which would constitute recognition
                    of the new Syrian Government (783.02/12–851).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
